{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S2a pushed for review as Gerrit change 1925 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1925).\n\nHeld-out oracle validated GREEN: restored the withheld edge/E2E tests (validation rejections, import isolation, non-terminating ParseError, alias/epilog composition) and folded them into the two file-impact-declared test files; full set = 38 passing. Gave the oracle teeth via mutation — terminating error() and disabled unknown_capability detection both drove held-out assertions RED, then restored to GREEN.\n\nTwo orchestrator reconciliations post-implementation:\n1. Dropped the subagent's per-file-ignores BLE001 carve-out in pyproject.toml; rewrote the immutability test to use pytest.raises(AttributeError) so no lint config change ships.\n2. Contract reconciliation on rebase onto current origin/main: the new bridge-vocabulary contract (test_help_overview_coverage.py::test_shipped_surfaces_name_no_retired_bridge_command) bans the retired token 'purge-bridge' from shipped package source. The registry had added a concrete Route('purge-bridge', retired=True) purely to exercise the retired mechanism. Removed it — the shipped ROUTES table now names no retired verb; the retired field/validation/derive-exclusion mechanism stays and is exercised on synthetic routes in the held-out validation oracle. Updated the hidden/retired test to assert route_for('purge-bridge') is None and no retired route ships (reinforcing the ban). Shadow-parity unaffected (retired routes were already excluded from derived sets)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787181948221256001,"uuid":"85f5348a-95d1-452c-ba27-8e0455dae0a0"}